      "id": "bug-018",
      "timestamp": "2026-03-27T23:30:00.000Z",
      "error_message": "Only first overlay text audible when playing back stitched narration (Xing header stripping was insufficient)",
      "file": "src/lib/audio-stitcher.ts",
      "root_cause": "Naive JS MP3 buffer concatenation fails because: (1) Xing/LAME VBR headers declare total frame count causing browsers to stop early, (2) synthetic silence frames have different encoding parameters than ElevenLabs output causing decoder confusion at frame boundaries. Stripping headers alone was insufficient — the frame parameter mismatch between silence and real audio remained.",
      "fix": "Replaced entire audio-stitcher with ffmpeg-static based implementation. Uses ffmpeg concat filter (decode + re-encode) with anullsrc for silence gaps. Produces a spec-compliant single MP3. Added ffmpeg-static to serverExternalPackages in next.config.ts.",
